1
00:00:02,397 --> 00:00:06,733
Water, earth,

2
00:00:06,818 --> 00:00:10,112
fire, air...

3
00:00:11,239 --> 00:00:15,284
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

4
00:00:15,368 --> 00:00:18,662
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

5
00:00:19,706 --> 00:00:23,625
Only the Avatar, master of all
four elements, could stop them.

6
00:00:23,710 --> 00:00:25,544
But when the world needed him most,

7
00:00:25,628 --> 00:00:26,920
he vanished.

8
00:00:27,338 --> 00:00:31,133
A hundred years passed, and my brother
and I discovered the new Avatar,

9
00:00:31,217 --> 00:00:32,801
an airbender named Aang.

10
00:00:32,885 --> 00:00:35,178
And although his
airbending skills are great,

11
00:00:35,263 --> 00:00:37,931
he has a lot to learn
before he's ready to save anyone.

12
00:00:38,891 --> 00:00:42,185
But I believe Aang can save the world.

13
00:00:54,490 --> 00:00:58,160
So, travelers,
the next time you think you hear

14
00:00:58,244 --> 00:01:00,579
a strange large bird talking,

15
00:01:00,663 --> 00:01:07,377
take a closer look. It might not be
a giant parrot, but a flying man,

16
00:01:08,004 --> 00:01:12,507
a member of a secret group
of airwalkers who laugh at gravity

17
00:01:12,592 --> 00:01:15,969
and laugh at those
bound to the earth by it.

18
00:01:17,930 --> 00:01:20,015
Aren't airbender stories the best?

19
00:01:20,099 --> 00:01:22,809
Was it realistic?
Is that how it was back then?

20
00:01:22,894 --> 00:01:24,853
I laugh at gravity all the time.

21
00:01:24,937 --> 00:01:27,064
Ha ha! Gravity.

22
00:01:27,148 --> 00:01:28,648
Jingle, jingle.

23
00:01:33,738 --> 00:01:34,988
Sorry.

24
00:01:35,073 --> 00:01:37,032
Aw. Cheapskates.

25
00:01:37,116 --> 00:01:38,909
Hey, thanks for the story.

26
00:01:38,993 --> 00:01:40,702
Tell it to the cap, boy.

27
00:01:45,041 --> 00:01:48,043
Aw. Much obliged, little bat thing.

28
00:01:48,127 --> 00:01:50,420
It means a lot
to hear airbender stories.

29
00:01:50,630 --> 00:01:52,214
It must have been a hundred years ago

30
00:01:52,423 --> 00:01:53,715
your great-grandpa met them.

31
00:01:53,800 --> 00:01:56,134
What are you prattling about, child?

32
00:01:56,219 --> 00:01:58,595
Great-grandpappy
saw the airwalkers last week.

33
00:02:07,230 --> 00:02:09,189
We're almost
to the Northern Air Temple.

34
00:02:09,732 --> 00:02:11,358
This is where
they had the championships

35
00:02:11,442 --> 00:02:12,609
for sky bison polo.

36
00:02:13,861 --> 00:02:16,488
Do you think
we'll really find airbenders?

37
00:02:16,572 --> 00:02:18,657
You want me to be like you
or totally honest?

38
00:02:18,741 --> 00:02:20,200
Are you saying I'm a liar?

39
00:02:20,284 --> 00:02:22,828
I'm saying you're an optimist.
Same thing, basically.

40
00:02:23,287 --> 00:02:25,080
Hey, guys, look at this!

41
00:02:34,048 --> 00:02:35,924
They really are airbenders!

42
00:02:37,677 --> 00:02:38,969
No, they're not.

43
00:02:39,053 --> 00:02:40,137
What do you mean, they're not?

44
00:02:40,221 --> 00:02:41,430
Those guys are flying!

45
00:02:41,848 --> 00:02:43,974
Gliding maybe, but not flying.

46
00:02:44,058 --> 00:02:45,183
You can tell by the way they move

47
00:02:45,268 --> 00:02:48,270
they're not airbending.
Those people have no spirit.

48
00:02:54,902 --> 00:02:57,487
I don't know, Aang.
That kid seemed pretty spirited.

49
00:03:09,959 --> 00:03:12,627
We'd better find some solid ground
before it finds us.

50
00:03:16,757 --> 00:03:18,133
Ha ha!

51
00:03:21,220 --> 00:03:22,554
Go, Teo!

52
00:03:22,638 --> 00:03:25,223
Show that bald kid how it's done!

53
00:03:41,032 --> 00:03:42,866
Hey there. You're pretty good.

54
00:03:43,075 --> 00:03:46,036
Yeah, I know.
But I can do more than fancy gliding.

55
00:04:02,094 --> 00:04:04,304
Wow! I don't think I can do that.

56
00:04:04,472 --> 00:04:05,972
But here's a good one.

57
00:04:28,079 --> 00:04:29,371
What do you think?

58
00:04:29,455 --> 00:04:30,580
It's great.

59
00:04:45,972 --> 00:04:49,391
Hey, you're a real airbender.

60
00:04:49,809 --> 00:04:51,935
You must be the Avatar.

61
00:04:52,019 --> 00:04:55,272
That's amazing!
I've heard stories about you.

62
00:04:55,648 --> 00:04:56,648
Thanks.

63
00:04:56,732 --> 00:04:59,067
Wow! This glider chair is incredible.

64
00:04:59,151 --> 00:05:01,194
If you think this is good,
wait until you see

65
00:05:01,279 --> 00:05:03,446
the other stuff my dad designed.

66
00:05:25,052 --> 00:05:26,636
Wow!

67
00:05:26,846 --> 00:05:28,763
Yeah, my dad is the mastermind

68
00:05:28,848 --> 00:05:30,348
behind this whole place.

69
00:05:30,600 --> 00:05:32,350
Everything is powered by hot air.

70
00:05:32,518 --> 00:05:34,019
It even pumps hot air currents outside

71
00:05:34,103 --> 00:05:35,645
to give us a lift when we're gliding.

72
00:05:35,855 --> 00:05:37,397
This place is unbelievable.

73
00:05:37,481 --> 00:05:39,190
Yeah. It's great, isn't it?

74
00:05:39,275 --> 00:05:41,318
No. Just unbelievable.

75
00:05:41,527 --> 00:05:43,945
Aang used to come here
a long time ago.

76
00:05:44,030 --> 00:05:46,948
I think he's a little shocked
it's so different.

77
00:05:47,283 --> 00:05:48,408
So better!

78
00:05:54,040 --> 00:05:57,000
This is supposed to be
the history of my people.

79
00:06:12,099 --> 00:06:14,976
I'm sure some parts of the temple
are still the same.

80
00:06:19,482 --> 00:06:21,483
It's nice to see at least
one part of the temple

81
00:06:21,567 --> 00:06:22,734
that isn't ruined.

82
00:06:33,454 --> 00:06:35,664
What the doodle? Don't you know enough

83
00:06:35,748 --> 00:06:38,124
to stay away from construction sites?

84
00:06:38,209 --> 00:06:40,502
We have to make room
for the bathhouse.

85
00:06:40,586 --> 00:06:42,087
Do you know what you did?

86
00:06:42,296 --> 00:06:44,339
You just destroyed something sacred

87
00:06:44,423 --> 00:06:46,132
for a stupid bathhouse.

88
00:06:46,217 --> 00:06:48,593
Well, people around here
are starting to stink.

89
00:06:48,678 --> 00:06:50,679
This whole place stinks.

90
00:06:50,763 --> 00:06:51,971
Hyah!

91
00:07:00,189 --> 00:07:03,566
This is a sacred temple.
You can't treat it this way.

92
00:07:03,776 --> 00:07:05,235
I've seen it when the monks were here.

93
00:07:05,319 --> 00:07:06,653
I know what it's supposed to be like.

94
00:07:06,737 --> 00:07:10,281
The monks? But you're 12.

95
00:07:10,366 --> 00:07:13,034
Dad, he's the Avatar.

96
00:07:13,119 --> 00:07:15,161
He used to come here
a hundred years ago.

97
00:07:15,246 --> 00:07:17,997
What are you doing?
Who said you could be here?

98
00:07:18,999 --> 00:07:20,375
Doing here...

99
00:07:20,584 --> 00:07:23,670
A long time ago,
but not a hundred years,

100
00:07:23,754 --> 00:07:26,005
my people became refugees

101
00:07:26,090 --> 00:07:27,966
after a terrible flood.

102
00:07:28,050 --> 00:07:31,469
My infant son, Teo, was badly hurt

103
00:07:31,554 --> 00:07:32,762
and lost his mother.

104
00:07:34,432 --> 00:07:36,474
I needed somewhere to rebuild,

105
00:07:36,642 --> 00:07:38,435
and I stumbled across this place.

106
00:07:38,561 --> 00:07:39,728
Couldn't believe it.

107
00:07:39,812 --> 00:07:43,857
Everywhere pictures of flying people,
but empty.

108
00:07:43,941 --> 00:07:45,150
Nobody home.

109
00:07:45,234 --> 00:07:48,570
Then I came across
these fan-like contraptions.

110
00:07:48,654 --> 00:07:49,821
Our gliders.

111
00:07:49,905 --> 00:07:52,490
Yes, little light flying machines.

112
00:07:52,575 --> 00:07:53,992
They gave me an idea...

113
00:07:54,076 --> 00:07:57,328
Build a new life for my son
in the air.

114
00:07:57,413 --> 00:08:00,331
Then everyone would be
on equal ground,

115
00:08:00,416 --> 00:08:02,208
so to speak.

116
00:08:02,585 --> 00:08:05,962
We're just in the process of
improving upon what's already here.

117
00:08:06,046 --> 00:08:10,216
And after all,
isn't that what nature does?

118
00:08:10,301 --> 00:08:12,093
Nature knows where to stop.

119
00:08:12,178 --> 00:08:13,678
I suppose that's true.

120
00:08:13,763 --> 00:08:19,142
Unfortunately, progress has a way
of getting away from us.

121
00:08:19,226 --> 00:08:20,435
Look at the time!

122
00:08:22,938 --> 00:08:25,690
Come. The pulley system
must be oiled before dark.

123
00:08:25,775 --> 00:08:28,193
Wait. How can you tell the time
from that thing?

124
00:08:28,277 --> 00:08:30,028
The notches all look the same.

125
00:08:30,112 --> 00:08:32,405
The candle will tell us. Watch.

126
00:08:34,533 --> 00:08:36,618
You put spark powder in the candle!

127
00:08:36,702 --> 00:08:40,455
Four flashes. So it's exactly
four hours past midday,

128
00:08:40,539 --> 00:08:42,665
or as I call it, four o'candle.

129
00:08:42,750 --> 00:08:43,792
Ha ha!

130
00:08:43,876 --> 00:08:45,043
If you liked that,

131
00:08:45,127 --> 00:08:48,129
wait till you see
my finger-safe knife sharpener.

132
00:08:48,214 --> 00:08:51,049
It only took me three tries
to get it right.

133
00:08:51,801 --> 00:08:53,718
Aah!

134
00:08:53,928 --> 00:08:55,053
Follow me.

135
00:08:55,137 --> 00:08:57,347
Hey, Aang,
I want to show you something.

136
00:08:58,390 --> 00:08:59,682
I just can't get over it.

137
00:08:59,767 --> 00:09:01,768
There's not a single thing
that's the same.

138
00:09:01,852 --> 00:09:03,353
I don't know about that.

139
00:09:03,437 --> 00:09:04,604
The temple might be different,

140
00:09:04,688 --> 00:09:07,857
but the creatures that live here are
probably direct descendants

141
00:09:07,942 --> 00:09:10,026
of the ones that lived here
a long time ago.

142
00:09:10,110 --> 00:09:13,655
You're right. They're kind of keepers
of the temple's origins.

143
00:09:15,032 --> 00:09:17,116
Besides, there is
one part of the temple

144
00:09:17,201 --> 00:09:18,409
that hasn't changed at all.

145
00:09:19,370 --> 00:09:20,370
Hey...

146
00:09:20,538 --> 00:09:22,580
It's just like the one
in the other air temple.

147
00:09:22,665 --> 00:09:24,499
Only an airbender can open it.

148
00:09:24,583 --> 00:09:26,709
So inside, it's completely untouched.

149
00:09:26,794 --> 00:09:28,127
Just the way the monks left it.

150
00:09:28,295 --> 00:09:31,005
I've always wondered
what it was like in there.

151
00:09:31,423 --> 00:09:32,465
Aang?

152
00:09:32,550 --> 00:09:35,051
I'm sorry.
This is the last part of the temple

153
00:09:35,135 --> 00:09:36,678
that's the same as it was.

154
00:09:36,762 --> 00:09:38,388
I want it to stay that way.

155
00:09:38,931 --> 00:09:41,099
I completely understand.

156
00:09:41,183 --> 00:09:42,851
I just wanted you to know it was here.

157
00:09:42,935 --> 00:09:44,227
Thanks.

158
00:09:49,984 --> 00:09:53,444
These lanterns are terrible.
I can't see.

159
00:09:53,988 --> 00:09:56,364
Why would you
want to use fireflies for light?

160
00:09:56,448 --> 00:09:59,367
Hey! Close that up. They'll get loose.

161
00:09:59,451 --> 00:10:02,871
Fireflies are
a nonflammable light source.

162
00:10:09,003 --> 00:10:11,129
Cover your nose and hold your breath.

163
00:10:12,798 --> 00:10:15,675
Ok. So you brought me
all the way down here

164
00:10:15,759 --> 00:10:16,968
to see an empty room.

165
00:10:17,177 --> 00:10:18,303
Wrong.

166
00:10:18,387 --> 00:10:21,431
It's filled to the brim
with natural gas.

167
00:10:21,515 --> 00:10:23,474
I came across it my first time here.

168
00:10:23,559 --> 00:10:26,477
Unfortunately, I was
carrying a torch at the time.

169
00:10:26,562 --> 00:10:30,398
Nearly blew myself and the whole place
even more sky-high.

170
00:10:30,482 --> 00:10:33,067
I thought my eyebrows
would never grow back.

171
00:10:33,152 --> 00:10:36,738
Anyway, there's a vital problem
that needs solving.

172
00:10:36,947 --> 00:10:40,033
From time to time, we have gas leaks.

173
00:10:40,117 --> 00:10:42,619
And they're nearly impossible to find.

174
00:10:42,912 --> 00:10:45,246
So this place is an explosion
waiting to happen.

175
00:10:45,456 --> 00:10:48,249
Yes. Until I figure out how to locate

176
00:10:48,334 --> 00:10:52,337
something I can't see,
hear, smell, or touch.

177
00:10:52,588 --> 00:10:54,088
The wind will carry you.

178
00:10:54,173 --> 00:10:55,673
It supports something inside you,

179
00:10:55,758 --> 00:10:57,342
something even lighter than air.

180
00:10:57,676 --> 00:11:00,219
And that something
takes over when you fly.

181
00:11:01,639 --> 00:11:02,889
I've changed my mind.

182
00:11:02,973 --> 00:11:05,099
I think I was born
without that something.

183
00:11:05,309 --> 00:11:08,144
Ha! Impossible. Everybody has it.

184
00:11:08,270 --> 00:11:09,354
Spirit.

185
00:11:09,521 --> 00:11:10,730
What?

186
00:11:10,814 --> 00:11:12,565
That's the something
you're talking about.

187
00:11:12,650 --> 00:11:13,942
Yeah. I suppose it is.

188
00:11:16,070 --> 00:11:17,070
Are you ready?

189
00:11:17,196 --> 00:11:19,864
No! Aah!

190
00:11:28,082 --> 00:11:30,166
I can't believe I'm flying!

191
00:11:30,250 --> 00:11:31,876
Just make sure
you keep your mouth closed

192
00:11:31,961 --> 00:11:33,211
so you don't swallow a bug.

193
00:11:35,965 --> 00:11:37,757
Teo was right about the air.

194
00:11:37,841 --> 00:11:39,509
All I had to do was trust it,

195
00:11:39,593 --> 00:11:41,260
let it carry me.

196
00:11:41,345 --> 00:11:43,221
Even though Teo's not an airbender,

197
00:11:43,305 --> 00:11:45,348
he really does have the spirit of one.

198
00:11:48,227 --> 00:11:49,352
I've been thinking.

199
00:11:49,436 --> 00:11:51,688
If you want to see
what's in that room,

200
00:11:51,897 --> 00:11:53,940
I'd be happy to open the door for you.

201
00:11:54,274 --> 00:11:56,109
- Great.
- Wait!

202
00:11:56,193 --> 00:11:57,610
How do I land this thing?

203
00:11:58,070 --> 00:11:59,404
What if I land over in the...

204
00:12:00,948 --> 00:12:03,658
Blech! Bug. bug.

205
00:12:03,742 --> 00:12:05,368
That was a bug.

206
00:12:09,832 --> 00:12:11,791
I said, don't touch anything.

207
00:12:13,669 --> 00:12:14,794
Don't worry.

208
00:12:14,878 --> 00:12:16,295
That experiment is old,

209
00:12:16,380 --> 00:12:19,799
and that egg was just
part of last week's lunch.

210
00:12:21,176 --> 00:12:23,011
Week-old egg smell.

211
00:12:23,095 --> 00:12:24,137
Quick, find that egg.

212
00:12:26,473 --> 00:12:29,225
I can't believe I'm finally
going to see what's inside.

213
00:12:42,281 --> 00:12:44,782
How could something that's so small,
you can't even see it,

214
00:12:44,867 --> 00:12:46,451
make such a big stink?

215
00:12:46,535 --> 00:12:49,287
That's the solution to our problem.

216
00:12:49,371 --> 00:12:52,248
Yeah. If we put a whole mess
of rotten eggs

217
00:12:52,458 --> 00:12:54,167
in the cellar
where the gas seeps up...

218
00:12:54,251 --> 00:12:57,545
The gas will mix
with the smell of rotten eggs.

219
00:12:57,629 --> 00:12:58,921
Then if there's a leak...

220
00:12:59,006 --> 00:13:00,840
You smell rotten eggs.

221
00:13:00,924 --> 00:13:02,633
Then you just follow your nose

222
00:13:02,718 --> 00:13:05,094
to the place where the smell
is coming from...

223
00:13:05,179 --> 00:13:07,430
And plug up the hole
where the gas is escaping.

224
00:13:07,514 --> 00:13:08,681
-You're a genius!
-You're a genius!

225
00:13:10,684 --> 00:13:12,602
Something is wrong. I've got to go.

226
00:13:26,533 --> 00:13:27,950
This is a nightmare.

227
00:13:28,577 --> 00:13:29,952
You don't understand.

228
00:13:30,871 --> 00:13:32,830
You're making weapons
for the Fire Nation.

229
00:13:41,423 --> 00:13:44,008
You make weapons for the Fire Nation?

230
00:13:45,844 --> 00:13:47,887
Explain all this... Now!

231
00:13:48,097 --> 00:13:50,807
It was about a year
after we moved here.

232
00:13:51,016 --> 00:13:54,393
Fire Nation soldiers
found our settlement.

233
00:13:54,478 --> 00:13:57,271
You were too young
to remember this tale.

234
00:13:57,481 --> 00:13:59,107
They were going to destroy everything,

235
00:13:59,191 --> 00:14:00,691
burn it to the ground.

236
00:14:00,776 --> 00:14:04,070
I pleaded with them.
I begged them to spare us.

237
00:14:04,154 --> 00:14:06,030
They asked what I had to offer.

238
00:14:06,281 --> 00:14:08,908
I offered my services.

239
00:14:09,159 --> 00:14:12,537
You must understand.
I did this for you.

240
00:14:22,798 --> 00:14:24,048
When are they coming?

241
00:14:24,842 --> 00:14:27,927
Soon, very soon.

242
00:14:28,053 --> 00:14:30,388
You can't give them more weapons.

243
00:14:30,472 --> 00:14:32,098
If I don't give them what they want,

244
00:14:32,182 --> 00:14:33,891
they will destroy this place.

245
00:14:36,395 --> 00:14:37,770
How can I be proud of you

246
00:14:37,855 --> 00:14:40,565
when your inventions
are being used for murder?

247
00:14:41,150 --> 00:14:42,984
I need some time to think.

248
00:14:44,695 --> 00:14:46,028
You need to leave. Go.

249
00:14:46,113 --> 00:14:47,613
We're not leaving.

250
00:14:47,698 --> 00:14:49,699
Then hide quickly.

251
00:14:53,620 --> 00:14:55,454
You know better
than to keep me waiting.

252
00:14:55,539 --> 00:14:58,207
Give me what you owe us
so I can be on my way.

253
00:14:59,668 --> 00:15:02,503
Well? Is there a problem?

254
00:15:03,297 --> 00:15:05,131
No. Right this way.

255
00:15:07,968 --> 00:15:09,510
The deal is off.

256
00:15:09,595 --> 00:15:10,761
The Avatar.

257
00:15:10,846 --> 00:15:12,722
Aang, don't get involved.

258
00:15:12,931 --> 00:15:14,724
If I don't get what I came for,

259
00:15:14,933 --> 00:15:17,727
the Fire Nation
will burn this place to rubble.

260
00:15:17,811 --> 00:15:19,228
Get out of here.

261
00:15:21,064 --> 00:15:22,732
You're leaving empty-handed.

262
00:15:22,816 --> 00:15:26,402
Then the destruction of this temple
will be on your head.

263
00:15:36,580 --> 00:15:38,497
This is bad, very bad.

264
00:15:38,582 --> 00:15:40,041
Aang, what are we gonna do?

265
00:15:40,125 --> 00:15:42,376
How can we possibly
keep them all away?

266
00:15:42,461 --> 00:15:43,628
I'll tell you how.

267
00:15:43,712 --> 00:15:45,171
We have something they don't...

268
00:15:45,255 --> 00:15:46,547
Air power.

269
00:15:46,632 --> 00:15:48,257
We control the sky.

270
00:15:48,342 --> 00:15:50,509
That's something
the Fire Nation can't do.

271
00:15:50,719 --> 00:15:52,053
We can win.

272
00:15:52,179 --> 00:15:53,304
I want to help.

273
00:15:54,765 --> 00:15:57,016
Good. We'll need it.

274
00:15:58,644 --> 00:16:00,478
We finally got
the war balloon working,

275
00:16:00,562 --> 00:16:01,938
thanks to Sokka.

276
00:16:02,147 --> 00:16:03,522
This boy is a genius.

277
00:16:03,732 --> 00:16:05,316
Thank you. You're a genius.

278
00:16:05,525 --> 00:16:06,734
Thank you.

279
00:16:07,110 --> 00:16:09,445
See, the problem
with the old war balloon was,

280
00:16:09,529 --> 00:16:10,863
you could get it airborne,

281
00:16:10,948 --> 00:16:13,282
but once you did, it just kept going.

282
00:16:13,367 --> 00:16:14,742
You could put a hole in the top,

283
00:16:14,826 --> 00:16:16,744
but then all the hot air would escape.

284
00:16:16,828 --> 00:16:20,831
So the question became,
how do you keep a lid on hot air?

285
00:16:20,999 --> 00:16:22,541
If only we knew.

286
00:16:24,628 --> 00:16:26,671
A lid is actually the answer.

287
00:16:26,797 --> 00:16:29,840
If you control the hot air,
you control the war balloon.

288
00:16:30,050 --> 00:16:32,927
That's actually pretty smart.

289
00:16:33,011 --> 00:16:34,971
Ok. We got four kinds of bombs...

290
00:16:35,180 --> 00:16:37,431
Smoke, slime, fire, and...

291
00:16:37,516 --> 00:16:38,683
Stink.

292
00:16:38,767 --> 00:16:41,269
Never underestimate
the power of stink.

293
00:16:48,068 --> 00:16:49,360
They're coming!

294
00:16:49,569 --> 00:16:50,736
Are we ready?

295
00:16:50,821 --> 00:16:53,239
Yes, but where's Sokka
with the war balloon?

296
00:16:53,323 --> 00:16:55,324
We'll have to start without it.

297
00:17:28,108 --> 00:17:29,108
Ooh!

298
00:17:37,617 --> 00:17:39,035
Take them out of the sky now!

299
00:18:02,601 --> 00:18:03,642
We've got them on the run.

300
00:18:03,852 --> 00:18:05,311
We need more slime.

301
00:18:12,486 --> 00:18:13,569
Aah!

302
00:18:44,851 --> 00:18:46,102
Whoa!

303
00:19:24,933 --> 00:19:26,851
Yaah!

304
00:19:39,948 --> 00:19:41,532
Those things are unstoppable.

305
00:19:41,616 --> 00:19:43,451
I think I know how they work.

306
00:19:43,535 --> 00:19:46,579
I remember my dad tinkering with
a counterbalancing system,

307
00:19:46,663 --> 00:19:48,080
something to do with water.

308
00:19:48,290 --> 00:19:49,582
Works great?

309
00:19:49,749 --> 00:19:52,209
Water? Can you get me close to one?

310
00:19:52,294 --> 00:19:53,294
No problem.

311
00:20:34,169 --> 00:20:35,836
We're out of bombs.

312
00:20:35,921 --> 00:20:39,131
Come on, Sokka.
Where's that war balloon?

313
00:20:48,517 --> 00:20:50,809
Hey, why aren't they shooting at us?

314
00:20:50,894 --> 00:20:52,186
The insignia.

315
00:20:52,270 --> 00:20:54,271
They think we're on their side.

316
00:20:54,356 --> 00:20:56,398
Then I guess
they won't see this coming.

317
00:20:56,483 --> 00:20:58,484
Bombs away.

318
00:20:59,486 --> 00:21:01,529
Hey! Aah!

319
00:21:06,159 --> 00:21:07,952
No. That was the last one.

320
00:21:09,538 --> 00:21:10,829
Wait a second.

321
00:21:10,914 --> 00:21:12,081
You smell that?

322
00:21:12,165 --> 00:21:14,041
Rotten eggs. There.

323
00:21:14,251 --> 00:21:15,876
That's where the gas is escaping.

324
00:21:21,841 --> 00:21:25,177
What are you doing?
That's our fuel source.

325
00:21:25,262 --> 00:21:27,096
It's the only bomb we've got.

326
00:21:48,326 --> 00:21:50,077
Look. They're retreating.

327
00:21:50,161 --> 00:21:51,662
Yeah!

328
00:21:51,746 --> 00:21:52,830
We're going down!

329
00:21:53,164 --> 00:21:55,124
No! Sokka, hold on!

330
00:21:56,418 --> 00:21:57,668
Get ready.

331
00:22:12,350 --> 00:22:13,350
You know what?

332
00:22:13,518 --> 00:22:15,686
I'm really glad
you guys all live here now.

333
00:22:15,895 --> 00:22:18,981
I realized it's like the hermit crab.

334
00:22:19,190 --> 00:22:20,899
Maybe you weren't born here,

335
00:22:21,109 --> 00:22:23,861
but you found this empty shell
and made it your home,

336
00:22:23,987 --> 00:22:25,904
and now you protect each other.

337
00:22:25,989 --> 00:22:28,032
That means a lot coming from you.

338
00:22:28,700 --> 00:22:30,868
Aang, you were right about air power.

339
00:22:30,952 --> 00:22:32,411
As long as we've got the skies,

340
00:22:32,495 --> 00:22:34,371
we'll have the Fire Nation on the run.

341
00:22:49,554 --> 00:22:53,932
This defeat is the gateway
to many victories.
